From 482fb4b3333a284127d74733b35f0af0e9b7fbf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:33:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Paired-episode analysis review fixes: read-only dump, D7-d
 settings, D8 shared states

- DecisionDumper is a pure observer: records policy argmax, expert and the
  executed action; EVAL.teacher_forcing removed (it recomputed the SPL
  expert per model, whose random.choice over merged-ghost positions and
  run-dependent RNG order could silently desynchronise the 'shared' states).
- Protocol 2 now uses the D8 replay (base walks the expert, try5/kd replay
  with per-step position/graph checks); protocol 1 is checked episode by
  episode against the D7-d evaluation with scripts/eval_d8/verify.py.
- dump_eval.sh wraps scripts/eval_d7/d7d_eval.sh, so checkpoints and every
  evaluation setting match D7-d/D8 (the previous launcher missed
  MODEL.policy_name R1Policy, used wrong baseline/try5/kd paths and omitted
  several D7-d overrides).
- Dump records front_cur per vp; the report classifies steps by the
  reference action (stop / backtrack / turn / straight) instead of a local
  option count that is >= 2 at nearly every ETP node; backtracks replace
  revisits; terminal forced stops are not scored; cross-run pairing checks
  position + graph signatures; feature-distribution section added.
- episode_features.py hides GPUs (CLIP would load on cuda:0);
  n_landmarks excludes environmental categories.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013viJtZsLciemzz8VtLkwa1
